freecell-solver needs its Perl modules in the build perl.

CMakeLists.txt checks for Moo with ${PERL_EXECUTABLE}, and the build runs
scripts/gen-*.pl, which load Moo, Path::Tiny and Template. Upstream lists
the modules only as DEPENDS, which in a cross build are target packages;
the build perl is the host tools perl, so CMake stopped at
CMakeLists.txt:246. Declare them as TOOL_DEPENDS as well.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- a/games/freecell-solver/Makefile
+++ b/games/freecell-solver/Makefile
@@ -16,6 +16,11 @@
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Moo-[0-9]*:../../devel/p5-Moo
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Path-Tiny-[0-9]*:../../filesystems/p5-Path-Tiny
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Template-Toolkit-[0-9]*:../../www/p5-Template-Toolkit
+# The CMake step runs Perl generators that load Moo, Path::Tiny and
+# Template with the build perl.
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Moo-[0-9]*:../../devel/p5-Moo
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Path-Tiny-[0-9]*:../../filesystems/p5-Path-Tiny
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Template-Toolkit-[0-9]*:../../www/p5-Template-Toolkit
 
 USE_LANGUAGES=	c c++
 USE_TOOLS+=	gmake perl
